Bruce wrote on Tue, 4 Nov 2003 21:17:51 +0000 (UTC):
> Yes, but why does nethack use the score to rank?  The general opinion of
> those who have ascended several times or more seems to be that score
> only matters before ascension.  To that extent, the scoring system is
> very effective.  It efficiently and accurately (enough) ranks the
> ability of each player.

> Once ascensions enter the mix, though, it falls apart.  High scores no
> longer reflect skill.  In fact, the opposite is frequently true.  To
> this extent, the scoring system is flawed.  

Cannot agree more. It would be a very interesting tournament, one
whose ranking is done in several disciplines which actually require
skill.

In the current one, I'm afraid the top prizes can be won only through
ultra-long boring games (the refinement of these techniques possibly
requires some skills as well, but that is not the point).

